# FIXED 2026-08-26 (the spread application rework: the snapshot waits
# for the settled source -- argsnap in driveStagedArgs/RefVal.find).
# Claim C4 (use-case 06): a generator over a map whose &: spread
# template contains a RELATIVE reference used to kill the whole model.
# The two ports: lines alone evaluated fine; adding any generator over
# $.ports (pack or each, even with an empty template) exited 1 -- the
# generator's early snapshot of the source carried the unresolved
# .containerPort, rebased where no root traversal reaches, and the
# generator never fired ([aontu/mapval_no_gen]). The data argument now
# snapshots its source only once the source has finished resolving in
# the tree, exactly as reference-language.md promises ("a generator's
# data can still be merged into by ... a spread after it first looks
# complete" -- generators wait for it). each() over the same source
# works too. Pinned in the shared spec: gen-pack.tsv
# pack-over-spread-augmented, gen-each.tsv each-over-spread-augmented.
# expected: {"out":{"a":{}},"ports":{"a":{"containerPort":1,"port":1}}}
# actual:   {"out":{"a":{}},"ports":{"a":{"containerPort":1,"port":1}}} exit 0
ports: { a: { containerPort: 1 } }
ports: &: { port: .containerPort }
out: pack($.ports, {})
